WP-006,happy_path,sec_rag,What are Apple’s key products mentioned in the filing?,"The Apple 2025 Form 10‑K lists the company’s primary product lines and specific models announced or current during fiscal 2025, including iPhone, Mac, iPad, and Wearables/Home & Accessories; the filing also documents fiscal‑year product announcements and Apple’s intellectual property posture [SEC-1][SEC-2][SEC-3].

Key findings:
- The filing identifies four primary product categories: iPhone (smartphones), Mac (personal computers), iPad (tablets), and Wearables, Home and Accessories (smartwatches, wireless headphones, spatial computers) [SEC-1].
- iPhone models explicitly listed in the filing include iPhone 17 Pro, iPhone Air, iPhone 17, iPhone 16 and iPhone 16e [SEC-1].
- Mac models explicitly listed include MacBook Air, MacBook Pro, iMac, Mac mini, Mac Studio and Mac Pro [SEC-1].
- iPad models explicitly listed include iPad Pro, iPad Air, iPad and iPad mini [SEC-1].
- Wearables, Home and Accessories examples called out include Apple Watch Series 11, Apple Watch SE 3, Apple Watch Ultra 3, AirPods (AirPods Pro, AirPods Max), Beats products, and Apple Vision Pro (spatial computer) [SEC-1].
- The company’s ‘Product, Service and Software Announcements’ for fiscal 2025 enumerate specific quarter-by-quarter launches and OS releases, including MacBook Pro, Mac mini, iMac, iPad mini, iPhone 16e, iPad Air, MacBook Air, Mac Studio, iPhone 17 family, Apple Watch Series 11 family, AirPods Pro 3, and OS updates (iOS 26, macOS Tahoe 26, iPadOS 26, watchOS 26, visionOS 26, tvOS 26) [SEC-2].
- The filing states Apple has accumulated a large portfolio of issued and registered intellectual property rights worldwide and believes the duration of those rights is adequate relative to its products’ expected lives [SEC-3].

Risk considerations:
- Company disclosures vs. external facts: the filing text lists product categories, models and announced releases but does not, in the provided excerpts, quantify product‑level revenue, unit volumes, pricing, or margins — those items are not present in the cited passages (data gap).
- Timing and scope: model names and announcements reflect Apple’s fiscal 2025 statements (report date 2025‑09‑27; filing accession 0000320193‑25‑000079). Confirm whether models or software releases changed after the 10‑K filing date before relying on them [SEC-1][SEC-2].
- Intellectual property: Apple discloses a large IP portfolio and states its belief that IP duration is adequate for product lives; this is a company assertion in the filing and not an independent legal opinion or guarantee [SEC-3].
- No implied financial inference: the product lists and announcements alone do not establish each product’s financial contribution, growth trajectory, market share, or risk exposure — those require additional financial and market data (missing from provided excerpts).

Next steps:
- If you want model‑level or timing detail, read the full Form 10‑K (accession 0000320193‑25‑000079) sections cited above, especially the ‘Products’ and ‘Product, Service and Software Announcements’ passages [SEC-1][SEC-2].
- To assess financial contribution by product, review Apple’s MD&A and segment disclosures in the full 10‑K and subsequent 10‑Q or 8‑K filings for product/segment revenue details (these were not included in the excerpts provided).
- For current product availability, specs, pricing or post‑filing updates, consult Apple press releases, recent SEC filings (10‑Q/8‑K) and reputable market data sources — the 10‑K reflects the company’s position at the filing/report dates [SEC-2].
- If you plan any investment or portfolio action, obtain live market data and seek advice from a licensed financial professional; this assembled summary uses only the cited SEC filing excerpts and is educational, not a recommendation.

Educational prototype only; not financial, investment, tax, or legal advice.",sec_rag_retriever,"[""supervisor_router"", ""company_financial_metrics"", ""sec_filing_search""]","[""market_research""]","[""market_research""]",False,False,ok,5,"[""Products\niPhone\niPhone® is the Company’s line of smartphones based on its iOS operating system.\nThe iPhone line includes iPhone 17 Pro, iPhone Air™, iPhone 17, iPhone 16 and\niPhone 16e.\nMac\nMac® is the Company’s line of personal computers based on its macOS® operating\nsystem. The Mac line includes laptops MacBook Air® and MacBook Pro®, as well as\ndesktops iMac®, Mac mini®, Mac Studio® and Mac Pro®.\niPad\niPad® is the Company’s line of multipurpose tablets based on its iPadOS®\noperating system. The iPad line includes iPad Pro®, iPad Air®, iPad and iPad\nmini®.\nWearables, Home and Accessories\nWearables includes smartwatches, wireless headphones and spatial computers. The\nCompany’s line of smartwatches, based on its watchOS® operating system, includes\nApple Watch® Series 11, Apple Watch SE® 3 and Apple Watch Ultra® 3. The\nCompany’s line of wireless headphones includes AirPods®, AirPods Pro®, AirPods\nMax® and Beats® products. Apple Vision Pro™ is the Company’s spatial computer"", ""Product, Service and Software Announcements\nThe Company announces new product, service and software offerings at various\ntimes during the year. Significant announcements during fiscal year 2025\nincluded the following:\nFirst Quarter 2025:\n•MacBook Pro\n•Mac mini\n•iMac\n•iPad mini\nSecond Quarter 2025:\n•iPhone 16e\n•iPad Air\n•iPad\n•MacBook Air\n•Mac Studio\nThird Quarter 2025:\n•iOS 26, macOS Tahoe 26, iPadOS 26, watchOS 26, visionOS 26 and tvOS 26\nFourth Quarter 2025:\n•iPhone 17, iPhone Air, iPhone 17 Pro and iPhone 17 Pro Max\n•Apple Watch Series 11, Apple Watch SE 3 and Apple Watch Ultra 3\n•AirPods Pro 3"", ""development, design and marketing, and is currently pursuing thousands of\napplications around the world. Over time,