WP-011,happy_path,fundamentals,Summarize Apple’s revenue trend using available company metrics.,"Apple's reported consolidated net sales increased from $383,285 million in fiscal 2023 to $391,035 million in fiscal 2024 and to $416,161 million in fiscal 2025, reflecting a modest acceleration in revenue growth in 2025 (6% year-over-year) after a 2% increase in 2024. Growth in 2025 was driven by Services (up 14%) and iPhone (up 4%), with notable strength in Mac and iPad and a decline in Wearables, Home and Accessories. Net income rose to $112,010 million in 2025. Regional performance was mixed: Greater China declined (lower iPhone sales), while Japan and Rest of Asia Pacific increased. Company facts provide operating cash flow, capital expenditures, and calculated free cash flow for 2025; live market prices and valuation multiples are not available in the returned filings.

Key findings:
- Total net sales: $416,161 million (FY2025) vs $391,035 million (FY2024) vs $383,285 million (FY2023); total net sales rose 6% in 2025 vs 2024 and 2% in 2024 vs 2023 [SEC-3].
- Product mix and year-over-year changes in 2025 vs 2024: iPhone $209,586 million (up 4%), Mac $33,708 million (up 12%), iPad $28,023 million (up 5%), Wearables, Home and Accessories $35,686 million (down 4%), Services $109,158 million (up 14%) — Services was the largest single product category by revenue in 2025 [SEC-3].
- Net income and comprehensive income: net income was $112,010 million in FY2025 (up from $93,736 million in FY2024); total comprehensive income was $113,611 million in FY2025 [SEC-2].
- Regional trends: Greater China net sales decreased in 2025 versus 2024 primarily due to lower iPhone sales; Japan and Rest of Asia Pacific net sales increased in 2025 driven by higher iPhone and Services (Japan also had higher iPad sales) [SEC-1].
- Deferred revenue: a portion of total net sales that had been previously deferred at the beginning of the period was $8,229 million for 2025 (compare $7,728 million in 2024 and $8,169 million in 2023) — indicates some revenue recognition timing effects in Services and other categories [SEC-3].
- Reported cash-flow and capital items in company facts (FY2025): net cash provided by operating activities $111,482 million; payments to acquire property, plant and equipment $12,715 million; calculated free cash flow (operating cash flow minus capex) $98,767 million; payments for repurchase of common stock $90,711 million. These figures come from the SEC company facts feed for Apple (accession 0000320193-25-000079) and are historical filing data (not live market data) [company facts accession 0000320193-25-000079].

Risk considerations:
- Company disclosure risks: Apple calls out regional variability (e.g., Greater China decline) and foreign-currency translation effects in other comprehensive income, which can cause volatility in reported results [SEC-1] [SEC-2].
- Product and revenue-concentration risk: Services grew fastest in 2025 (14%), but hardware categories (especially iPhone) remain large and can be cyclical; Wearables declined in 2025, showing category-level variability [SEC-3].
- Accounting and timing effects: A non-trivial portion of net sales was previously deferred at the beginning of each period ($8,229 million in 2025), so year-over-year revenue comparisons are affected by revenue-recognition timing [SEC-3].
- Data and scope gaps: the returned evidence is historical filing data (annual FY2025, FY2024, FY2023) and does not include live market prices, forward guidance, segment-level margins beyond top-line sales, or detailed cash-flow statement passages in the extracted SEC excerpts — these are necessary to form a fuller operational and valuation view [company facts accession 0000320193-25-000079].
- Scenario assumption risk: the year-over-year percentage changes reported here are simple historical comparisons (period-over-period); they do not imply future growth rates or forecasts and do not account for macroeconomic scenarios, product-cycle timing, or competitive shifts.

Next steps:
- Review Apple’s MD&A (management discussion & analysis) and segment disclosures in the full 10-K for FY2025 to understand drivers of Services growth, hardware unit/price trends, and margin dynamics (requires human review of the full filing beyond the extracted passages) [SEC-3] [SEC-2].
- If you need up-to-date valuation or trade decisions, obtain current market prices and consensus forward estimates from a live market data source; the SEC company facts used here are historical and do not include market prices [company facts accession 0000320193-25-000079].
- Assess cash-flow quality and capital allocation by reviewing the full consolidated statements of cash flows and notes to the financial statements in the 10-K to confirm operating cash flow, capex, and share-repurchase timing and policy (human review required) [SEC-2] [company facts accession 0000320193-25-000079].
- If regional exposure matters to your analysis (e.g., Greater China sensitivity), consider stress-testing revenue for scenarios where iPhone sales in Greater China remain weaker or recover, and review any management commentary on regional risk mitigation [SEC-1].
- For investment decisions or portfolio action, consult a qualified financial professional who can combine these historical filing facts with current market data, personal circumstances, and suitability analysis (this report is educational and not a recommendation).

