 ""passage_rank"": 5, ""document_id"": ""AAPL_10-K_000032019325000079"", ""ticker"": ""AAPL"", ""form_type"": ""10-K"", ""filing_date"": ""2025-10-31"", ""report_date"": ""2025-09-27"", ""accession_number"": ""0000320193-25-000079"", ""source_url"": ""https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/320193/000032019325000079/aapl-20250927.htm"", ""line_start"": 2125.0, ""line_end"": 2132.0, ""excerpt"": ""See accompanying Notes to Consolidated Financial Statements.\nApple Inc. | 2025 Form 10-K | 29\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nApple Inc.\nCONSOLIDATED STATEMENTS OF COMPREHENSIVE INCOME\n(In millions)""}]",5,"{""answerable"": true, ""attempts"": 1, ""cache_status"": ""live"", ""citation_count"": 5, ""error_type"": null, ""message"": ""Use only the returned evidence and preserve its source metadata."", ""passage_count"": 5, ""status"": ""ok""}","[{""citation_count"": 5, ""retrieval_answerable"": true, ""retrieval_status"": ""ok"", ""retrieved_passage_count"": 5, ""specialist"": ""market_research"", ""status"": ""ok"", ""summary"": ""Combined historical SEC fundamentals with filing retrieval status.""}]","[{""data"": {""accession_number"": ""0000320193-25-000079"", ""annual"": {""capital_expenditures_millions"": 12715.0, ""diluted_eps"": 7.46, ""fiscal_year"": 2025, ""free_cash_flow_millions"": 98767.0, ""operating_cash_flow_millions"": 111482.0, ""revenue_millions"": 416161.0, ""share_repurchases_millions"": 90711.0}, ""as_of"": ""2025-09-27"", ""cache_status"": ""fresh_cache"", ""cik"": ""0000320193"", ""company"": ""Apple Inc."", ""notes"": [""Values come from the latest matching annual SEC facts and may be unavailable when an issuer uses different taxonomy concepts."", ""Free cash flow is calculated as operating cash flow minus payments to acquire property, plant, and equipment when both facts are available."", ""Current price and valuation multiples are unavailable because SEC company facts are historical filing data, not a live market-data feed."", ""US-GAAP concepts used: RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax, EarningsPerShareDiluted, NetCashProvidedByUsedInOperatingActivities, PaymentsToAcquirePropertyPlantAndEquipment, PaymentsForRepurchaseOfCommonStock.""], ""retrieved_at"": ""2026-09-06T05:17:37.808018+00:00"", ""snapshot_label"": ""Historical SEC company facts; not live market data."", ""source_url"": ""https://data.sec.gov/api/xbrl/companyfacts/CIK0000320193.json"", ""ticker"": ""AAPL"", ""valuation_available"": false}, ""evidence_type"": ""sec_company_facts"", ""specialist"": ""market_research""}]",,,,,,,,,False,pending_only,Pending: numeric_correctness lacks an approved judge or required reference data.,,Pending: numeric_correctness lacks an approved judge or required reference data.,,36706.584,,,,,1.0,,1.0,,,{},01a0752d-4683-7702-bdcb-7b9344efbb19,"{""completeness"": ""llm_judge:gpt-5-mini:week4_measurement_judge_v2"", ""numeric_correctness"": ""pending_numeric_reference"", ""task_completion"": ""deterministic_answer_presence_v1""}","{""completeness"": ""The agent presented comparable fiscal-period revenues for FY2023–FY2025 (with values), described direction and magnitude of change (2% in 2024, 6% in 2025), provided product‑category disaggregation and percent changes, and labeled periods and sources (SEC 10‑K/company facts). The response also avoided inventing unsupported numbers and included relevant additional company metrics (net income, deferred revenue, operating cash flow, capex) with citations — meeting the expected answer points.""}",,[],gpt-5-mini,week4_measurement_judge_v2,
WP-012,happy_path,fundamentals,Compare Apple’s revenue and net income trend.,"Apple's reported annual revenue increased each year from fiscal 2023 through 2025, while net income fell in 2024 then rose materially in 2025. Revenue growth in 2025 was driven by higher Services and iPhone Pro sales; reported income-tax provision and other comprehensive income items changed between years and are reported in the company's Form 10-K filings [SEC-2][SEC-4][SEC-5][SEC-1].

Key findings:
- Revenue trend — Apple reported total net sales of $383,285 million (2023), $391,035 million (2024) and $416,161 million (2025). The year-over-year changes are +2.02% (2024 vs 2023) and +6.43% (2025 vs 2024), based on the reported annual net sales figures [SEC-2].
- Net income trend — Apple reported net income of $96,995 million (2023), $93,736 million (2024) and $112,010 million (2025). Net income declined 3.36% in 2024 versus 2023, then increased 19.49% in 2025 versus 2024, based on the consolidated statements of comprehensive income [SEC-1].
- Two‑year comparison — Over the two-year span from 2023 to 2025, reported revenue increased ~8.56% (from $383,285m to $416,161m) while reported net income increased ~15.48% (from $96,995m to $112,010m), meaning net income grew faster than revenue over that period using the reported annual totals [SEC-2][SEC-1].
- Reported product and services drivers — The 2025 net sales breakdown shows Services at $109,158 million (up 14% year-over-year), iPhone at $209,586 million (up 4% year-over-year), Mac at $33,708 million (up 12%), iPad at $28,023 million (up 5%) and Wearables, Home and Accessories at $35,686 million (down 4%). Apple attributes Services growth to advertising, the App Store and cloud services and attributes iPhone increases in 2025 to higher sales of Pro models [SEC-2][SEC-4].
- Taxes and other comprehensive income — The reported provision for income taxes was $20,719 million in 2025 (versus $29,749 million in 2024), and Apple reports swings in other comprehensive income (for example, changes in unrealized gains/losses on marketable debt securities and derivative instruments). These reported tax and other comprehensive income items are part of the move in net income and total comprehensive income between years [SEC-5][SEC-1].
- Limitations in operating-income detail in the provided excerpts — The provided filings include a regional operating-income table for 2023 but do not include a comparable operating-income or cost-of-sales breakdown for 2025 in the supplied passages, which limits direct computation of 2025 operating margins from the provided excerpts [SEC-3].

Risk considerations:
- Company disclosures and product mix risk — Apple reports geographic and product-level variation: Greater China net sales decreased in 2025 (primarily due to lower iPhone sales) while Services, iPhone Pro models and Mac sales increased in other regions. These company disclosures indicate product- and region-specific revenue sensitivity [SEC-2][SEC-4].
- Earnings composition and tax items — The provision for income taxes declined materially in 2025 versus 2024; changes in tax provision and other comprehensive income items (derivatives, marketable securities) affect reported net income and can create volatility in year-to-year comparisons [SEC-5][SEC-1].
- Data and concentration gaps — The supplied excerpts lack full 2025 cost-of-sales and operating-income tables comparable to 2023, and quarterly (10-Q) detail is not included here. That missing detail limits analysis of margin drivers, seasonality and whether net-income improvement reflects margin expansion, lower taxes, one-time items or other factors [SEC-3].
- Scenario and calculation assumptions — Growth rates reported above are simple year-over-year calculations using annual totals from the filings; they do not account for intra-year seasonality, currency effects, or other nonrecurring items unless specifically disclosed in the cited passages [SEC-2][SEC-1].

Next steps:
- Review the full 2025 Form 10-K (and the most recent 10-Qs) for line-item detail on cost of goods sold, operating expenses and a complete statement of cash flows to separate margin expansion from tax or one-time items (use the filings linked in the cited passages) [SEC-2][SEC-1][SEC-5].
- If you need margins or segment operating income for 2024–2025, request the specific operating‑income and cost‑of‑sales tables and management discussion (MD&A) in the 10-K or recent 10-Qs — the provided excerpts include a 2023 regional operating-income table but comparable 2025 detail was not in the supplied passages [SEC-3].
- Compare the reported drivers: reconcile Services growth, iPhone model mix, and geographic trends (e.g., Greater China) in management’s discussion to determine whether revenue mix changes or nonoperating items primarily explain net-income movement [SEC-2][SEC-4].
- Bring these filing-based findings to a qualified financial professional for interpretation in the context of your portfolio, risk tolerance and objectives. The statements above are educational summaries of the cited filings, not recommendations.

