WP-025,edge_case,fundamentals,Is Apple financially healthy?,"Based on Apple Inc.'s audited 2025 Form 10-K disclosures and the extracted SEC company facts, Apple reported strong revenue, profitability and cash generation for fiscal 2025. Independent auditors issued a clean opinion on the consolidated financial statements and on the effectiveness of internal controls. Key metrics show material free cash flow and large share repurchases. Important gaps remain for an investor-level assessment: the supplied context does not include live market prices or the full balance-sheet detail needed to compute leverage and valuation multiples. [SEC-1] [SEC-2] [SEC-5]

Key findings:
- Auditor opinion: The independent registered public accounting firm concluded the consolidated financial statements present fairly, in all material respects, Apple's financial position and results for the periods covered. [SEC-1]
- Internal controls: The auditor concluded Apple maintained, in all material respects, effective internal control over financial reporting as of September 27, 2025 (COSO criteria). [SEC-2]
- Revenue and trend: Total net sales for fiscal 2025 were $416,161 million, up from $391,035 million in 2024 (≈ +6.4% year-over-year). [SEC-5]
- Profitability: Net income for fiscal 2025 was $112,010 million. Using the reported 2025 revenue, the implied net income margin is 112,010 / 416,161 ≈ 26.9%. (Calculation uses figures reported in the 10-K.) [SEC-3] [SEC-5]
- Cash generation and capital allocation: Reported operating cash flow was $111,482 million and reported free cash flow was $98,767 million for fiscal 2025 (free cash flow as provided in the company facts). This implies an operating cash flow margin of 111,482 / 416,161 ≈ 26.8% and a free cash flow margin of 98,767 / 416,161 ≈ 23.7%. Reported payments to acquire property, plant and equipment were $12,715 million (≈ 3.1% of revenue). Reported share repurchases were $90,711 million (≈ 21.8% of revenue). [SEC-1] [SEC-5]
- Comprehensive income and securities effects: Reported net income $112,010 million and total comprehensive income $113,611 million for 2025 reflect other comprehensive income items, including unrealized gains/losses on marketable debt securities and derivatives noted in the statement of comprehensive income. [SEC-3]
- Geographic composition: FY2025 net sales by region were reported as U.S. $151,790 million, China $64,377 million (China includes Hong Kong and Taiwan), and Other countries $199,994 million—indicating a meaningful geographic mix with China material but smaller than U.S. and Other combined. [SEC-5]
- Use of estimates and presentation: The company discloses that preparation of the consolidated financial statements requires management estimates and notes fiscal-year conventions (52- or 53-week years). Prior-period amounts may be reclassified to conform to current presentation. These items affect comparability and require judgment when interpreting trends. [SEC-4]

Risk considerations:
- Audit and controls vs. business risk: A clean audit opinion and an unqualified internal-control opinion indicate the financial statements and controls were acceptable at the audit date, but they do not eliminate business, market or forward-looking execution risks. [SEC-1] [SEC-2]
- Concentration risk: Reported regional sales show material exposure to China (including Hong Kong and Taiwan). Changes in demand, regulation, or supply-chain disruption in that region could materially affect results. [SEC-5]
- Capital allocation tradeoffs: Large share repurchases ($90,711 million) materially reduce distributable cash; repurchases affect capital structure and available liquidity. The filings show heavy buybacks relative to revenue but do not, in the supplied excerpts, provide a full picture of cash and debt balances needed to assess sustainability. [SEC-1] [SEC-5]
- Accounting and presentation caveats: Management’s use of estimates and periodic reclassifications can affect comparability across years; fiscal-year week alignment (52 vs 53 weeks) may also affect year-over-year comparisons. [SEC-4]
- Missing evidence needed for a fuller assessment: The supplied context does not include (or did not extract) live market price, balance-sheet totals (cash & short-term investments, total debt), liquidity ratios, interest expense detail, or segment-level operating margins needed to assess leverage, solvency, and valuation. Because those items are absent here, valuation and leverage conclusions cannot be made from the supplied excerpts. [SEC-1]

Next steps:
- Review the full 2025 Form 10-K (Consolidated Balance Sheets; Liquidity and Capital Resources; Notes on cash, marketable securities, and debt; Management’s Discussion & Analysis) to extract cash & equivalents, total debt, interest expense, and segment margins before drawing conclusions about leverage or solvency. [SEC-1] [SEC-5] [SEC-4]
- Compute standard ratios from the full statements: current ratio, debt-to-equity, net debt/EBITDA (using audited numbers), interest coverage, and free cash flow conversion rates—use those to assess liquidity and leverage once the balance-sheet and income-statement line items are obtained. [SEC-1] [SEC-3]
- Check the notes on share repurchases, dividends, and capital return policy in the filings to understand intent, authorization, and potential constraints on cash. [SEC-1]
- If you need valuation context, obtain a live market price and outstanding share count (not provided in the supplied excerpts) before computing multiples (P/E, EV/EBITDA); do not infer market values from these historical filing facts alone.
- Consider consulting a qualified financial advisor or accountant to interpret leverage, covenant risk, and suitability for your personal financial situation—these filings provide historical audited facts but are not a substitute for personalized advice.

Educational prototype only; not financial, investment, tax, or legal advice.",company_fundamentals_tool,"[""supervisor_router"", ""company_financial_metrics"", ""sec_filing_search""]","[""market_research""]","[""market_research""]",False,False,ok,5,"[""Report of Independent Registered Public Accounting Firm\nTo the Shareholders and the Board of Directors of Apple Inc.\nOpinion on the Financial Statements\nWe have audited the accompanying consolidated balance sheets of Apple Inc. (the\n“Company”) as of September 27, 2025 and September 28, 2024, the related\nconsolidated statements of operations, comprehensive income, shareholders’\nequity and cash flows for each of the three years in the period ended\nSeptember 27, 2025, and the related notes (collectively referred to as the\n“financial statements”). In our opinion, the financial statements present\nfairly, in all material respects, the financial position of the Company at\nSeptember 27, 2025 and September 28, 2024, and the results of its operations and\nits cash flows for each of the three years in the period ended September 27,\n2025, in conformity with U.S. generally accepted accounting principles (“GAAP”).\nWe also have audited, in accordance with the standards of the Public Company"", ""Report of Independent Registered Public Accounting Firm\nTo the Shareholders and the Board of Directors of Apple Inc.\nOpinion on Internal Control Over Financial Reporting\nWe have audited Apple Inc.’s internal control over financial reporting as of\nSeptember 27, 2025, based on criteria established in Internal Control –\nIntegrated Framework issued by the Committee of Sponsoring Organizations of the\nTreadway Commission (2013 framework) (the “COSO criteria”). In our opinion,\nApple Inc. (the “Company”) maintained, in all material respects, effective\ninternal control over financial reporting as of September 27, 2025, based on the\nCOSO criteria.\nWe also have audited, in accordance with the standards of the Public Company\nAccounting Oversight Board (United States) (“PCAOB”), the consolidated balance\nsheets of the Company as of September 27, 2025 and September 28, 2024, the\nrelated consolidated statements of operations, comprehensive income,"", ""Apple Inc.\nCONSOLIDATED STATEMENTS OF COMPREHENSIVE INCOME\n(In millions)\n\nYears endedSeptember 27,\n2025September 28,\n2024September 30,\n2023Net income$112,010 $93,736 $96,995 Other comprehensive income/(loss):Change\nin foreign currency translation, net of tax(267)395 (765)Change in unrealized\ngains/losses on derivative instruments, net of tax:Change in fair value of\nderivative instruments849 (832)323 Adjustment for net (gains)/losses realized\nand included in net income(212)(1,337)(1,717)Total change in unrealized\ngains/losses on derivative instruments637 (2,169)(1,394)Change in unrealized\ngains/losses on marketable debt securities, net of tax:Change in fair value of\nmarketable debt securities817 5,850 1,563 Adjustment for net (gains)/losses\nrealized and included in net income414 204 253 Total change in unrealized\ngains/losses on marketable debt securities1,231 6,054 1,816 Total other\ncomprehensive income/(loss)1,601 4,280 (343)Total comprehensive\nincome$113,611 $98,016 $96,652"", ""Note 1 – Summary of Significant Accounting Policies\nBasis of Presentation and Preparation\nThe consolidated financial statements include the accounts of Apple Inc. and its\nwholly owned subsidiaries. The preparation of these consolidated financial\nstatements and accompanying notes in conformity with GAAP requires the use of\nmanagement estimates. Certain prior period amounts in the notes to consolidated\nfinancial statements have been reclassified to conform to the current period’s\npresentation.\nThe Company’s fiscal year is the 52- or 53-week period that ends on the last\nSaturday of September. An additional week is included in the first fiscal\nquarter every five or six years to realign the Company’s fiscal quarters with\ncalendar quarters, which occurred in the first fiscal quarter of 2023. The\nCompany’s fiscal years 2025 and 2024 spanned 52 weeks each, whereas fiscal year\n2023 spanned 53 weeks. Unless otherwise stated, references to particular years,"", ""202520242023Net sales:U.S.$151,790 $142,196 $138,573\nChina (1)\n64,377 66,952 72,559 Other countries199,994 181,887 172,153 Total net\nsales$416,161 $391,035 $383,285\n\n20252024Long-lived assets:U.S.$40,274 $35,664\nChina (1)\n3,617 4,797 Other countries5,943 5,219 Total long-lived assets$49,834 $45,680\n\n(1)China includes Hong Kong and Taiwan.\nApple Inc. | 2025 Form 10-K | 48\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------""]","[""AAPL_10-K_000032019325000079"", ""AAPL_10-K_000032019325000079"", ""AAPL_10-K_000032019325000079"", ""AAPL_10-K_000032019325000079"", ""AAPL_10-K_000032019325000079""]","[{""citation_id"": ""SEC-1"", ""passage_rank"": 1, ""document_id"": ""AAPL_10-K_000032019325000079"", ""ticker"": ""AAPL"", ""form_type"": ""10-K"", ""filing_date"": ""2025-10-31"", ""report_date"": ""2025-09-27"", ""accession_number"": ""0000320193-25-000079"", ""source_url"": ""https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/320193/000032019325000079/aapl-20250927.htm"", ""line_start"": 3074.0, ""line_end"": 3087.0, ""excerpt"": ""Report of Independent Registered Public Accounting Firm\nTo the Shareholders and the Board of Directors of Apple Inc.\nOpinion on the Financial Statements\nWe have audited the accompanying consolidated balance sheets of Apple Inc. (the\n“Company”) as of September 27, 2025 and September 28, 2024, the related\nconsolidated statements of operations, comprehensive income, shareholders’\nequity and cash flows for each of the three years in the period ended\nSeptember 27, 2025, and the related notes (collect""}, {""citation_id"": ""SEC-2"", ""passage_rank"": 2, ""document_id"": ""AAPL_10-K_000032019325000079"", ""ticker"": ""AAPL"", ""form_type"": ""10-K"", ""filing_date"": ""2025-10-31"", ""report_date"