WP-031,edge_case,multi_tool,"Use my portfolio and Apple filing to explain risk, but I did not upload holdings.","You did not upload holdings, so I used the fixed five‑holding demonstration portfolio you allowed. That demo portfolio has a total market value of $795,500, an unrealized gain of $120,500 (17.85% unrealized return), and heavy concentration in Technology: AAPL and MSFT each represent about 37.7% of the portfolio and Technology is ~75.4% of the portfolio. Apple’s most recent SEC annual filing (Form 10‑K for the fiscal year ended September 27, 2025, filed October 31, 2025) shows the company’s reported annual revenue, earnings per share, cash flows, capex, free cash flow and large share repurchases referenced below [SEC-2][SEC-1][SEC-5]. Important data gaps: no live market prices or valuation multiples are available from the SEC company facts, and I did not receive your real portfolio holdings — the analysis below is educational and based on the demo portfolio and filing evidence.

Key findings:
- Demo portfolio totals and return: total market value $795,500, total cost basis $675,000, unrealized gain $120,500, unrealized return 0.178519 (17.85%). (Source: demo portfolio analysis.)
- Position size and weights (demo): AAPL market value $300,000 (37.71% of portfolio); MSFT market value $300,000 (37.71%); VTI $100,000 (12.57%); BND $50,500 (6.35%); JNJ $45,000 (5.66%). (Source: demo portfolio analysis.)
- Concentration flags derived from the demo portfolio: AAPL >25% position threshold; MSFT >25% position threshold; Technology sector exposure ≈75.4% (above 40% sector threshold). (Source: demo portfolio analysis.)
- Apple SEC filing summary (Form 10‑K, fiscal year ended 2025‑09‑27): reported annual revenue $416,161 million; diluted earnings per share $7.46; net cash provided by operating activities $111,482 million; capital expenditures $12,715 million; calculated free cash flow $98,767 million; share repurchases (annual) $90,711 million. These figures come from Apple’s reported annual SEC facts for the 2025 fiscal year. [SEC-1]
- Filing and market details: Apple’s Form 10‑K is dated and filed for the fiscal year ended September 27, 2025 (filed October 31, 2025) [SEC-2]; Apple common stock is traded on The Nasdaq Stock Market LLC under the symbol AAPL, and the filing discloses share repurchase activity and the number of shareholders of record as of October 17, 2025 (22,429 holders of record). [SEC-5]
- Where to find the accounting detail in the 10‑K: consolidated balance sheets and related notes appear in the filing (see Consolidated Balance Sheets) [SEC-4] and shareholders’ equity rollforwards appear in the Consolidated Statements of Shareholders’ Equity [SEC-3].

Risk considerations:
- Portfolio concentration risk (demo): Two single positions (AAPL and MSFT) each near 37.7% creates high single‑name risk and correlated sector exposure (Technology ≈75.4%). This increases sensitivity to adverse outcomes affecting large-cap technology names. (Source: demo portfolio analysis.)
- Company‑disclosed items from Apple’s 10‑K may affect risk: the filing reports substantial share repurchases during the period (reported repurchases figure) which can affect share count and capital allocation; see the Issuer Purchases of Equity Securities section and related disclosures in the 10‑K for specifics. [SEC-5]
- Accounting and liquidity signals in the filing: Apple’s SEC facts report large operating cash flow, capex, and a sizeable calculated free cash flow for fiscal 2025, which are inputs to assessing corporate financial strength but do not substitute for forward valuation or market liquidity data. [SEC-1]
- Limits of available evidence and scenario assumptions: SEC company facts are historical filing data and do not provide live market prices or valuation multiples; the fundamentals snapshot is from the latest annual filing and may use SEC taxonomy concepts that differ across periods. The portfolio analysis used fixed illustrative demo prices rather than live market quotes. These limitations mean we cannot calculate current market valuations, forward returns, or real‑time exposure. [SEC-1] (and demo portfolio warnings).
- Missing personal and portfolio evidence: you did not upload your real holdings, risk profile, objectives, or time horizon. The demo portfolio is an illustrative substitute but may not reflect your actual positions, cash needs, tax situation, or suitability considerations. (Source: user-provided context and portfolio_analysis warnings.)

Next steps:
- Upload your actual holdings, cost basis, and the date(s) of those holdings so analysis can use real positions and current market quotes (requires your action).
- If you want to examine Apple further, review these 10‑K sections in the filing: (a) Consolidated Balance Sheets [SEC-4], (b) Consolidated Statements of Shareholders’ Equity [SEC-3], and (c) Item 5 disclosures for share repurchases and market/holder data [SEC-5].
- Confirm live market prices and valuations before making any allocation decisions — SEC company facts alone do not provide current market prices or multiples [SEC-1].
- If you are concerned about concentration, consider (for educational review) scenario analyses that estimate portfolio sensitivity to specified percent declines in AAPL and MSFT (I can run illustrative stress scenarios once you provide actual holdings and a chosen scenario).
