WP-032,edge_case,multi_tool,Compare my portfolio to Apple’s risk factors.,"This educational review compares the demo portfolio concentration in Apple (AAPL) to Apple Inc.'s disclosed risk factors and selected SEC-filed facts. The demo portfolio holds AAPL at $300,000 (37.7% of $795,500), leaving the portfolio highly concentrated in technology (75.4%). Apple’s 2025 Form 10‑K discloses macroeconomic and counterparty risks that can materially affect its financial condition and stock price [SEC-1]; the filing also shows historical company performance and financing disclosures referenced below [SEC-2][SEC-3][SEC-5]. Important data gaps: live market prices and the investor’s goals, risk tolerance, and time horizon are not provided in the materials reviewed.

Key findings:
- Portfolio concentration: The demo portfolio total market value is $795,500. AAPL position market value is $300,000, representing 37.7121% of the portfolio (portfolio weight 0.377121). Technology (AAPL + MSFT) is 75.4243% of the portfolio and exceeds typical 40% sector concentration thresholds flagged in the analysis.
- Portfolio performance snapshot: The demo portfolio’s total unrealized gain is $120,500 on a cost basis of $675,000, an unrealized return of 17.8519% (120,500 / 675,000). AAPL’s unrealized gain in the demo portfolio is $60,000 on a cost basis of $240,000.
- Company financial facts (historical SEC company facts): For Apple’s fiscal 2025 (historical filing facts), reported revenue was $416,161 million; diluted EPS was 7.46; net cash provided by operating activities was $111,482 million; capital expenditures were $12,715 million; calculated free cash flow (operating cash flow minus PPE purchases) was $98,767 million; and share repurchases were $90,711 million. These are historical SEC company facts in the retrieved dataset (company facts accession referenced) [SEC-2].
- Apple’s disclosed macro/financial risks: Apple’s Form 10‑K states that adverse economic conditions can increase credit and collectibility risk on trade receivables, cause failures of derivative counterparties and other financial institutions, limit Apple’s ability to issue new debt, reduce liquidity, and cause declines in the fair values of the Company’s financial instruments — any of which can materially adversely affect Apple’s business, results of operations, financial condition and stock price [SEC-1].
- General uncertainty disclosure: Apple’s 10‑K notes that uncertainties that differ from management’s expectations could have a material impact on the Company’s financial condition and operating results [SEC-4].
- Financing / debt disclosures: The filings list multiple note issuances (examples shown in the filing excerpts include notes due 2028, 2030, 2032/2033 and 2035/2053 with stated coupon rates in the exhibits), indicating the company uses debt markets and has outstanding notes described in SEC exhibits [SEC-5].
- Historical shareholder return as presented in the filing: Apple included a five‑year cumulative total shareholder return comparison (dividend‑reinvested basis), with the filing showing the company’s indexed values across 2020–2025 relative to the S&P 500 and a technology index — the filing highlights past performance but warns that past stock price performance is not necessarily indicative of future performance [SEC-3].
- Data gaps and limitations: The analysis uses fixed illustrative demo prices and historical SEC company facts; live market prices, current valuations, and up‑to‑date market cap or beta are not available in the provided materials. The investor’s objective, risk tolerance, and time horizon were not provided, preventing goal-aligned conclusions.

Risk considerations:
- Company-disclosed risks (from Apple’s 2025 Form 10‑K): The filing explicitly links adverse economic/financial conditions to higher credit risk, counterparty failure risk, reduced liquidity, limitations on issuing new debt, and declines in fair value of financial instruments — each of these can materially affect Apple’s stock price and financial condition [SEC-1].
- Concentration risk in the demo portfolio: AAPL is 37.7% of the demo portfolio and Technology represents 75.4% of the portfolio; concentration magnifies the portfolio’s exposure to AAPL-specific and technology-sector shocks (the demo portfolio’s volatility will be driven disproportionately by AAPL and MSFT).
- Leverage and financing risk channel: Apple’s use of debt markets (notes and exhibits shown in filings) means interest rate moves, credit spreads, or Apple‑specific credit developments could influence the company’s financing costs and investor perception — a possible channel for equity downside cited in the 10‑K exhibits [SEC-5].
- Scenario and model assumptions: The portfolio calculations are based on fixed illustrative demo prices (not live). Historical company facts (revenue, EPS, cash flow, buybacks) are from previously filed SEC company facts and are not forecasts; they describe past performance only [SEC-2].
- Missing evidence that matters: No live price, no current market capitalization, no forward-looking analyst estimates, and no investor objective/horizon are in the supplied materials. Those missing items limit any assessment of how an AAPL move would translate to a real‑time portfolio outcome.

Next steps:
- Obtain current market prices and position quantities for the portfolio (to recompute up‑to‑date weights and P&L using live data). Note: the supplied analysis used fixed demo prices and is educational only.
- If you want to explore portfolio sensitivity, run simple scenario analyses (examples: 10% and 25% declines in AAPL) to show the hypothetical impact on portfolio market value and weight — these require current prices and position sizes to be meaningful.
- Review Apple’s full 2025 Form 10‑K (the excerpts cited here are from that filing) and any more recent quarterly filings or 8‑K disclosures to check for new material developments, especially regarding liquidity, credit exposures, or significant off‑balance sheet items [SEC-1][SEC-4][SEC-5].
- Map this concentration exposure to your personal objectives and time horizon with a qualified human advisor: deciding whether to reduce concentration, hedge, or maintain exposure requires judgment about goals, taxes, trading costs, and risk tolerance (none of which were supplied).
- If desired, request an updated, goal‑driven portfolio review that includes live prices, current market caps, implied diversification changes, and stress tests tied to specific investor time horizons and liquidity needs.

Educational prototype only; not financial, investment, tax, or legal advice.",router plus relevant tools,"[""supervisor_router"", ""company_financial_metrics"", ""sec_filing_search"", ""portfolio_analytics""]","[""portfolio_analysis"", ""market_research""]","[""market_research"", ""portfolio_analysis""]",False,False,ok,5,"[""insolvency.\nAdverse economic conditions can also lead to increased credit and collectibility\nrisk on the Company’s trade receivables; the failure of derivative\ncounterparties and other financial institutions; limitations on the Company’s\nability to issue new debt; reduced liquidity; and declines in the fair values of\nthe Company’s financial instruments. These and other impacts can materially\nadversely affect the Company’s business, results of operations, financial\ncondition and stock price.\nApple Inc. | 2025 Form 10-K | 5"", ""therComprehensiveIncomeMember2022-09-252023-09-300000320193us-gaap:AccumulatedOtherComprehensiveIncomeMember2025-09-270000320193aapl:IPhoneMember2024-09-292025-09-270000320193aapl:IPhoneMember2023-10-012024-09-280000320193aapl:IPhoneMember2022-09-252023-09-300000320193aapl:MacMember2024-09-292025-09-270000320193aapl:MacMember2023-10-012024-09-280000320193aapl:MacMember2022-09-252023-09-300000320193aapl:IPadMember2024-09-292025-09-270000320193aapl:IPadMember2023-10-012024-09-280000320193aapl:IPadMember2022-09-252023-09-300000320193aapl:WearablesHomeandAccessoriesMember2024-09-292025-09-270000320193aapl:WearablesHomeandAccessoriesMember2023-10-012024-09-280000320193aapl:WearablesHomeandAccessoriesMember2022-09-252023-09-3000003201932025-09-282025-09-2700003201932026-09-272025-09-2700003201932027-09-262025-09-2700003201932028-10-012025-09-270000320193us-gaap:RestrictedStockUnitsRSUMember2022-09-252023-09-300000320193us-gaap:CashMember2025-09-270000320193us-gaap:MoneyMarketFundsMemberus-ga"", ""--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nCompany Stock Performance\nThe following g