WP-033,known_failure,sec_rag,Give me exact Apple revenue numbers from the filing.,"You asked for exact Apple revenue numbers from the filing. The companyreported totals and disaggregated net sales for fiscal years 2025, 2024 and 2023 in its 2025 Form 10-K. Below are the exact figures (in millions) as reported in the filing and short calculations of each product and region share. All filing claims cite the matching SEC passage ID.

Key findings:
- Total net sales (reported): 2025: $416,161; 2024: $391,035; 2023: $383,285. [SEC-2]
- Disaggregated net sales by product (2025 / 2024 / 2023, in millions): iPhone: $209,586 / $201,183 / $200,583; Mac: $33,708 / $29,984 / $29,357; iPad: $28,023 / $26,694 / $28,300; Wearables, Home and Accessories: $35,686 / $37,005 / $39,845; Services: $109,158 / $96,169 / $85,200. [SEC-2]
- Portion of total net sales that was included in deferred revenue at the beginning of the period (in millions): 2025: $8,229; 2024: $7,728; 2023: $8,169. [SEC-2]
- Geographic net sales (2025 / 2024 / 2023, in millions): U.S.: $151,790 / $142,196 / $138,573; China (includes Hong Kong and Taiwan): $64,377 / $66,952 / $72,559; Other countries: $199,994 / $181,887 / $172,153. Total net sales matches $416,161 / $391,035 / $383,285. [SEC-4] 
- Selected calculated shares of 2025 total net sales (calculations based on reported 2025 amounts): iPhone = $209,586 of $416,161 ≈ 50.4% (product share). [SEC-2]; Services = $109,158 of $416,161 ≈ 26.2% (product share). [SEC-2]; U.S. geographic share = $151,790 of $416,161 ≈ 36.5%. [SEC-4]

Risk considerations:
- All figures are historical, taken from Apples Form 10-K for the fiscal year ended September 27, 2025; they are not live market prices or forward-looking projections. [SEC-2] [SEC-4]
- The filing excerpts provided are limited to selected tables and passages (product and geographic sales, certain tax and operating lines). Additional notes, accounting policy detail, and context may exist elsewhere in the full filing and could affect interpretation. (See the consolidated financial statements reference.) [SEC-5]
- Company disclosures indicate foreign pretax earnings and tax provision detail for 2025-2023; those are distinct line items and not included in the product/region totals above. Example: foreign pretax earnings were $82.0 billion in 2025. [SEC-1]
- Concentration considerations: iPhone and Services together represent a majority of reported 2025 net sales based on the filing numbers above; this is a filing-based concentration observation, not an investment recommendation. [SEC-2]
- Data gaps in the supplied context: no post-2025 period data, no live share price or valuation multiples, no full set of footnotes or quarterly (10-Q) updates in the provided excerpts, and limited disclosure beyond the quoted tables. The specialist outputs also note that SEC company facts are historical company filing data and not a live market-data feed.

Next steps:
- If you need confirmation or the full context, open Apples complete 2025 Form 10-K (accession 0000320193-25-000079) and review the Notes to the Consolidated Financial Statements for accounting policies and deferred revenue detail. Relevant passages above are cited as [SEC-2], [SEC-4], [SEC-1], [SEC-5].
- For more recent results (after FY2025) check Apples subsequent Form 10-Q filings and any later 10-K; the supplied excerpts do not include post-2025 periods.
- If you want derived metrics (growth rates, margins, per-share metrics, or trend charts), identify which specific calculations you want and I will compute them using only the filing figures you authorize me to use.
- For financial decisions or suitability assessments based on these numbers, consult a qualified financial advisor; the above is an educational assembly of reported filing figures and calculations, not investment advice.

